# 🚀 FindMeAJob.com — Deep Dive Project Analysis

> **Project Concept:** A lightweight, no-login, frontend-only job search aggregator that runs automation to find relevant jobs from platforms like LinkedIn, Naukri, and others — based on user inputs — and displays results with download options.

---

## 1. 📋 Fields to Ask Users (Job Search Form)

### 🔵 Core Required Fields
These are the **minimum viable inputs** your automation engine needs to produce relevant results:

| Field | Type | Why It's Needed |
|---|---|---|
| **Full Name** | Text | For personalization only (local storage) |
| **Job Title / Role** | Text (with suggestions/autocomplete) | Primary search keyword — most critical field |
| **Experience Level** | Dropdown | Filters entry-level vs senior roles |
| **Skills** | Tags/Multi-select | Refines job matching beyond title |
| **Preferred Location(s)** | Text / Multi-select | Location-based filtering on platforms |
| **Work Mode** | Dropdown (Remote / Hybrid / On-site) | Increasingly critical filter |
| **Resume Upload** | File (PDF/DOCX) | For auto-fill and skill extraction |

### 🟡 Secondary Fields (Strongly Recommended)
| Field | Type | Why It's Needed |
|---|---|---|
| **Preferred Job Type** | Dropdown (Full-time / Part-time / Internship / Contract) | Filters job type on platforms |
| **Expected Salary / CTC** | Range Slider or Text | Filters salary bands |
| **Notice Period** | Dropdown (Immediate / 15 days / 30 days / 60 days / 90 days) | Naukri specifically supports this |
| **Industry / Domain** | Dropdown (IT / Finance / Healthcare / Marketing, etc.) | Domain-specific search refinement |
| **Education Qualification** | Dropdown | B.Tech / MBA / BCA / etc. — used in Naukri filters |
| **Current Company / College** | Text | Optional — for better context |

### 🟢 Auto-Fill from Resume (Parse & Pre-populate)
When user uploads a resume, auto-extract:
- Name, Email, Phone
- Skills (keyword extraction)
- Experience in years
- Current/last job title
- Education qualification

> **Tech approach:** Use `pdf.js` or `mammoth.js` (for DOCX) to extract raw text, then use regex/NLP patterns to identify fields. No backend needed.

### 🔴 Fields to Avoid (Complexity vs Value)
- Date of birth (privacy concern, adds no value)
- Photograph (unnecessary for job search)
- Detailed work history (too much effort for the user at this stage)

