## 4. ⚠️ Limitations of Each Platform

### 🔴 Critical Limitations (Affects Your Architecture Heavily)

| Platform | Limitation | Impact | Workaround |
|---|---|---|---|
| **LinkedIn** | Requires login to view full job details | High | Redirect user to the listing page (they log in themselves) |
| **LinkedIn** | No public scraping API, aggressive bot detection | High | URL-only approach |
| **LinkedIn** | 25 jobs shown max without login | Medium | Encourage login on LinkedIn itself |
| **Naukri** | Bot detection (Cloudflare) blocks scraping | High | URL deep-link only |
| **Naukri** | Some filters require account (apply button) | Medium | Redirect to listing page |
| **Indeed** | Deprecated their public job search API in 2021 | High | URL-only |
| **Indeed** | Anti-scraping CAPTCHAs | High | URL-only |
| **Glassdoor** | Login wall for job details | High | URL redirect |
| **All Platforms** | CORS policy blocks cross-origin fetch from browser | Critical | **Cannot scrape directly from browser frontend** |

### 🟡 The Core Technical Limitation
> **You CANNOT scrape job data directly from the browser frontend.** All major job platforms block cross-origin requests (CORS), use bot detection (Cloudflare, reCAPTCHA), and require authenticated sessions for full data access. This is a **hard technical boundary** that affects the entire "automation" strategy.

